{:edb/db-before-t 2601 :edb/db-after-t 2602 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535914 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:32:42.074Z" 13194139535914 true] [17592186166895 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374113 13194139535914 true] [17592186166895 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374123 13194139535914 true] [17592186166896 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374093 13194139535914 true] [17592186166896 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374133 13194139535914 true] [17592186166896 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374152 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374094 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374100 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374106 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1089 "q-340628" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1100 "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}+3$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1113 #uuid "343a6182-7115-5e27-a302-023217925f51" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374093 1145 "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374095 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374096 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374097 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374098 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374099 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1041 "field-1" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374097 13194139535914 true] [17592186374094 1110 #uuid "e002da2f-d308-571c-8ca0-8f8495b1def5" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374095 1034 "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535914 true] [17592186374095 1111 #uuid "6c7d8b42-e19d-5039-84bf-5898a99158f0" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374096 1034 "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535914 true] [17592186374096 1111 #uuid "8357f3b7-1498-5605-8849-2106401fe69e" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374097 1034 "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535914 true] [17592186374097 1111 #uuid "8fc361f5-7214-5f98-9680-d777eef3109f" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374098 1034 "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535914 true] [17592186374098 1111 #uuid "7e2d6348-6bd4-5940-b5e2-94ecbe8182bb" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374099 1034 "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" 13194139535914 true] [17592186374099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186